1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,321
Hi! This is GhostWatch: a séance for software. Summon an AI agent into a real cloud

2
00:00:07,321 --> 00:00:11,856
computer, and everyone watches it build your idea, live.

3
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:18,962
The problem: coding agents are black boxes. You can't follow or steer them, they run

4
00:00:18,962 --> 00:00:24,260
where one bad command does real damage, a crash loses everything, and nobody else

5
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:24,915
can watch.

6
00:00:26,517 --> 00:00:32,309
Our solution: the ghost, an OpenAI agent, possesses a fresh Freestyle VM and builds

7
00:00:32,309 --> 00:00:38,171
there. Everything streams live to every viewer. Anyone can throw curses to steer it.

8
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:44,033
The Exorcist blocks anything dangerous. And state lives in a Terse durable actor, so

9
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,429
it survives crashes.

10
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:52,034
Browsers connect over WebSocket to one Terse durable actor, the Ghost, whose

11
00:00:52,034 --> 00:00:57,345
persisted state syncs to everyone automatically. A disposable Bun worker runs the

12
00:00:57,345 --> 00:01:02,854
agent against OpenAI, executes tools in the Freestyle VM, and writes every step back

13
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:03,706
to the actor.

14
00:01:05,317 --> 00:01:10,574
The agents talk only through the actor. Spectators' curses queue there and pass the

15
00:01:10,574 --> 00:01:15,325
Exorcist; the ghost's tool results flow back and are broadcast to everyone.

16
00:01:16,927 --> 00:01:22,444
The code is small on purpose: the actor, a server with a supervisor, the agent loop

17
00:01:22,444 --> 00:01:27,895
with the Exorcist, and a Freestyle vessel with an offline mock. Let's see it live.

18
00:01:30,685 --> 00:01:36,711
This is the live séance. Two browsers are connected right now — mine, and a second

19
00:01:36,711 --> 00:01:41,341
spectator — both as WebSockets on the same Terse durable actor.

20
00:01:41,591 --> 00:01:47,277
Left: the ghost's live stream. Right: the portal where its app will appear, and the

21
00:01:47,277 --> 00:01:49,607
curse panel any spectator can use.

22
00:01:49,857 --> 00:01:53,409
I make a wish, and summon the ghost.

23
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:06,421
The worker just booted a brand-new Freestyle VM in under a second. The ghost — an

24
00:02:06,421 --> 00:02:10,474
OpenAI agent — is now inside it, checking which runtimes exist.

25
00:02:10,724 --> 00:02:15,916
Every thought, command and output is appended to the durable actor, which pushes it

26
00:02:15,916 --> 00:02:20,732
to every viewer instantly. The agents talk through the actor, never directly.

27
00:02:21,732 --> 00:02:27,106
We're fast-forwarding through the model's thinking time. Everything you see is real

28
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:27,948
and unedited.

29
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:36,857
It just wrote the entire app into the VM — you can see the file land in the stream.

30
00:02:37,107 --> 00:02:42,679
Now the other spectator throws a curse: make it rain bats. It travels over their

31
00:02:42,679 --> 00:02:47,067
WebSocket into the actor. On its next turn the ghost must obey.

32
00:02:47,317 --> 00:02:52,466
Someone malicious tries to curse the ghost into running rm -rf. The Exorcist

33
00:02:52,466 --> 00:02:58,089
intercepts it — destructive commands, secrets and prompt injections never reach the

34
00:02:58,089 --> 00:02:59,173
agent or the VM.

35
00:02:59,423 --> 00:03:06,479
Now the scary part. I kill -9 the worker process, mid-build.

36
00:03:06,729 --> 00:03:12,268
The browser stays connected to the actor. The wish, the step, the VM id and pending

37
00:03:12,268 --> 00:03:14,337
curses are all persisted there.

38
00:03:14,587 --> 00:03:20,915
The worker comes back, finds a haunting in progress, and re-enters the exact same

39
00:03:20,915 --> 00:03:22,243
VM. Nothing lost.

40
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:28,155
While it finishes, notice the ghost narrating in character. That narration is the

41
00:03:28,155 --> 00:03:30,461
real model output, streamed live.

42
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:37,359
The ghost published its app on a public HTTPS URL, served straight from the

43
00:03:37,359 --> 00:03:38,511
Freestyle VM.

44
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:44,723
While the model thinks, nothing is polling. The actor pushes each change to every

45
00:03:44,723 --> 00:03:46,975
browser the moment it is persisted.

46
00:03:47,453 --> 00:03:53,967
Here it is, full screen: a real app, built live by an AI agent in a cloud VM, while

47
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:55,301
everyone watched.

48
00:03:55,551 --> 00:03:58,719
Anyone can open this link right now.

49
00:03:58,969 --> 00:04:06,172
And the whole séance — log, curses, VM — lives on in the durable actor, ready for

50
00:04:06,172 --> 00:04:07,417
the next wish.

51
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:16,583
To run it: start the Terse actor server, install the client, add your OpenAI and

52
00:04:16,583 --> 00:04:24,042
Freestyle keys, run bun server dot ts, and open localhost 8790 in two browsers.

53
00:04:24,042 --> 00:04:29,046
Wish, summon, curse, and open the public portal link.

54
00:04:30,663 --> 00:04:38,367
GhostWatch: durable ghosts, real VMs, live AI. Happy Halloween!
